{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"92c3b591defad44ecc73414d358689250bc7ced51094c392362e724b8a462c34","digest":{"component_or_area":"gate-sidecar error handling","key_entities":["gate_dispatch.py","plan_review/sidecar.py","completion_sidecar.py","gate_error_v1","LLMUnavailableError","build_error_payload","reconcile_verdict","REVIEW_RESULT","COMPLETION_VERDICT","produce_plan_review_verdict","produce_code_review_verdict","produce_completion_verdict","latest_review_result","latest_fail_verdict"],"problem_keywords":["infrastructure exception","error verdict","gate sidecar","infra diagnosis","LLMUnavailableError","error tracking"],"propositions":["Infrastructure exceptions (LLMUnavailableError) at gate sites must emit an additive ERROR sidecar record with gate_error_v1 schema, cause, and evidence_ref without changing the gate's existing outcome.","Plan-review and code-review gates must write the ERROR record then return their existing degraded INDETERMINATE verdict; completion gate must write the ERROR record then re-raise the exception.","The gate_error_v1 schema must be routed separately and never pass through reconcile_verdict so the ERROR verdict is preserved and not coerced to FAIL.","Existing verdict readers (latest_review_result, latest_fail_verdict) must skip gate_error_v1 records due to schema guards and not surface ERROR records to callers.","Non-infrastructure domain exceptions (BLOCK/FAIL) must not generate ERROR sidecar records."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787689198805708001,"uuid":"eec3d04e-b9c3-444b-b809-a763e6ed8fbb"}